WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:03.930
The One Piece manga just revealed 3 things
that no one expected.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:09.840
The ancient Robot from the Void Century attacked
the celestial dragons just 200 years ago,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.260
Vegapunk has possibly the new most OP Devil
Fruits in the Story and it looks like the

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:19.949
genius scientist will join the straw hats
on their ship once they leave Egghead island.

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:22.890
But how likely is that actually?

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:26.220
Really, not that unlikely at all.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.660
Why does Vegapunk want to leave this place?

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.860
Egghead island seems incredibly small compared
to most of the islands we have been to recently.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.850
Dressrosa had an entire city on it, Tottland
was a whole archipelago and Wano multiple

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.719
islands mushed together.

00:00:41.719 --> 00:00:44.239
Egghead island looks tiny in comparison.

00:00:44.239 --> 00:00:48.520
It’s really only Vegapunks giant lab and
a bit of greenery around it.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:54.129
But despite its size, it’s an island that
seems to hold way more importance than almost

00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:56.800
any other place the straw hats have gone to.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.199
It is filled to the brim with the most advanced
technology in existence right now, holding

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:03.620
all the knowledge remaining from the ancient
kingdom.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:08.270
It’s the place where pretty much all major
technological advancements for the government

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:13.150
have been created, including the Pacifista
and Seraphim.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:18.110
The island holds pretty much all of Vegapunk's
research and knowledge, so why would he want

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:20.360
to go?

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.940
Because it turns out that this island isn’t
only Vegapunk’s base of operation, but in

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:27.930
a way a part of himself.

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:32.360
The Manga has now revealed that the scientist
is actually a devil fruit user, which does

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:37.020
explain his ridiculously large head in a reassuring
way.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.200
Vegapunk has eaten the brains brains fruit,
which in Japanese is called the Nomi Nomi

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.200
no mi.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:48.330
Which is hilarious, but Oda really had to
make this one work.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:54.549
Brain in Japanese is No, and brains, as in
having brains, being smart is called nomizu,

00:01:54.549 --> 00:02:00.270
so Oda decided to cut the zu to get to his
nomi nomi no mi, which is incredibly funny

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.710
and one of those puns that only work in Japanese.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.190
It seems like this fruit’s ability isn’t
high intelligence however.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.770
Apparently Vegapunk was born a real genius.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:15.720
Instead, the fruit allows its user to store
and remember any type of knowledge down to

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.739
the very last detail.

00:02:17.739 --> 00:02:21.489
That means anything you want to learn, you
know by heart in an instant.

00:02:21.489 --> 00:02:26.590
You always have access to all your knowledge
at any time and you never forget anything.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:31.600
A side-effect of the fruit, is that one’s
brain needs to keep growing the more knowledge

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.690
one acquires, in order to keep up with everything.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:37.420
Thus Vegapunk’s bizarre appearance.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.540
Now before we can discuss, what that has to
do with Vegapunk wanting to sail with Luffy,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:47.180
I think we have to discuss this fruit in more
detail, because:

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.909
This ability is just absolutely overpowered.

00:02:53.523 --> 00:02:58.563
If you have the ability to learn anything
you like without ever forgetting any of it,

00:02:58.563 --> 00:03:04.342
this would make you the most powerful person
in the world in no time.

00:03:04.342 --> 00:03:08.623
You could say: Oh, knowing stuff doesn’t
mean you can actually do anything against

00:03:08.623 --> 00:03:13.043
someone like Blackbeard with his Gura Gura
no mi or his darkness fruit.

00:03:13.043 --> 00:03:14.773
But that’s just not true.

00:03:14.773 --> 00:03:16.653
Just look at Vegapunk.

00:03:16.653 --> 00:03:21.513
Using his powers, he has deciphered all the
knowledge available from the ancient kingdom.

00:03:21.513 --> 00:03:23.163
He has created giant Robots.

00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:24.383
Lazer weapons.

00:03:24.383 --> 00:03:28.143
He has discovered how to use sea stone to
nullify devil fruit powers.

00:03:28.143 --> 00:03:31.682
And he can literally clone devil fruits.

00:03:31.682 --> 00:03:37.443
If Vegapunk wanted, he could just build an
army of Seraphim for himself and take over

00:03:37.443 --> 00:03:38.703
the world.

00:03:38.703 --> 00:03:43.083
When you have read every strategy and psychology
book in existence, when you know everything

00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:51.113
that is to know about anyone: In my eyes,
this makes you pretty close to invincible.

00:03:51.113 --> 00:03:54.113
Knowledge is power, as they like to say.

00:03:54.113 --> 00:04:00.242
Vegapunk is already intelligent and has exclusive
access to advanced knowledge, which makes

00:04:00.242 --> 00:04:05.953
his fruit even more potent than it would already
be if someone like luffy ate it.

00:04:05.953 --> 00:04:11.293
This man has literally managed to create alter
egos connected to a central brain.

00:04:11.293 --> 00:04:15.943
In fact, when you really think about just
HOW strong this fruit makes him, I am really

00:04:15.943 --> 00:04:21.293
wondering how Oda will nerf it, because let’s
be real he will have to.

00:04:21.293 --> 00:04:24.683
Why work with the government at this point,
if you could just overthrow them with your

00:04:24.683 --> 00:04:25.683
technology?

00:04:25.683 --> 00:04:28.963
I mean we already know that Vegapunk seems
to share the same cause as Dragon.

00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:34.383
My only real explanation, is that the government
has something up its sleeve, that Vegapunk

00:04:34.383 --> 00:04:36.483
can’t go up against openly.

00:04:36.483 --> 00:04:42.553
Either they have a way to hold him hostage,
which would be incredibly effective.

00:04:42.553 --> 00:04:47.962
Or, another explanation might be, that the
Gorosei and Imu have access to an ancient

00:04:47.962 --> 00:04:51.803
technology even MORE advanced than Vegapunk's.

00:04:51.803 --> 00:04:56.973
The type of technology that allowed them to
overthrow the technologically advanced ancient

00:04:56.973 --> 00:04:59.503
kingdom in the first place.

00:04:59.503 --> 00:05:03.023
If you have any ideas, I’d LOVE to hear
them.

00:05:03.023 --> 00:05:08.223
Because presented with its powers the nomi
nomi no mi does sound like the most powerful

00:05:08.223 --> 00:05:09.673
devil fruit in existence.

00:05:09.673 --> 00:05:14.783
Now I’m only curious if Vegapunk could clone
his Nomi Nomi no mi to make more nomi nomi

00:05:14.783 --> 00:05:23.552
no mis and give them to each of his clones
to multiply the effect.

00:05:23.552 --> 00:05:28.613
But maybe this immense power is exactly the
reason why the government is now coming for

00:05:28.613 --> 00:05:29.613
his head.

00:05:29.613 --> 00:05:32.953
Because they fear that he could surpass them.

00:05:32.953 --> 00:05:37.863
Anyways, as a side effect of consuming the
entire library of ohara and all the knowledge

00:05:37.863 --> 00:05:43.163
stored inside it, Vegapunk’s brain has grown
too large to carry around with him any longer.

00:05:43.163 --> 00:05:47.173
You know what, maybe that was the original
weak point of that fruit.

00:05:47.173 --> 00:05:52.053
That at some point it would just break your
neck or crush its user under its own weight.

00:05:52.053 --> 00:05:58.443
But Vegapunk found a way to separate his brain
and connect himself and all of his alter egos

00:05:58.443 --> 00:06:00.932
remotely to it.

00:06:00.932 --> 00:06:05.953
The at this point unfathomably large brain
is incorporated in the upper levels of his

00:06:05.953 --> 00:06:08.503
lab, labeled the Punk Records.

00:06:08.503 --> 00:06:13.834
He actually dreams of connecting every person
in the world to this pool of knowledge, which

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:18.613
sounds like a nice idea, kind of like the
internet of the one piece world.

00:06:18.613 --> 00:06:23.473
However Jinbei raises some really important
privacy concerns here.

00:06:23.473 --> 00:06:28.063
Because giving everyone access to Vegapunks
brain, like the other Vegapunks, wouldn’t

00:06:28.063 --> 00:06:31.073
that turn everyone into vegapunk?

00:06:31.073 --> 00:06:37.033
It would also mean everyone would know everything
about everyone all the time, which does sound

00:06:37.033 --> 00:06:40.283
like something out of a black mirror episode
if you ask me.

00:06:40.283 --> 00:06:44.923
Vegapunk sweeps this comment aside, saying
that science needs to keep acvancing.

00:06:44.923 --> 00:06:51.133
And I think that might hint at Vegapunk’s
biggest character flaw: He puts scientific

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:53.983
advance over his morals.

00:06:53.983 --> 00:06:58.663
Clearly Vegapunk agrees with Dragon’s plans
and dislikes the government.

00:06:58.663 --> 00:07:03.033
But getting funding for his research was more
important to him.

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:08.783
Similarly he, Cesar, Judge and Queen were
conducting ethically highly questionable research

00:07:08.783 --> 00:07:10.443
on humans and prisoners.

00:07:10.443 --> 00:07:13.432
Killing many and disfiguring others.

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:17.313
Look at the emotionless vinsmoke family or
the giants on punk hazard.

00:07:17.313 --> 00:07:23.242
I think Vegapunk is not a bad guy at heart,
but his priority make him a quite morally

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.423
ambiguous character.

00:07:25.423 --> 00:07:30.503
Same as the people who have watched this video
so far, but haven’t subscribed to the channel

00:07:30.503 --> 00:07:31.503
yet.

00:07:31.503 --> 00:07:37.383
now all this also fits in very nicely with
the reveal, that Vegapunk is also a perfectionist.

00:07:37.383 --> 00:07:41.693
He deemed Momo’s fruit a failure because
the color didn’t match.

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:47.723
Or the lightsaber, that actually works like
the ones in star wars, because they also attract

00:07:47.723 --> 00:07:49.602
bugs.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:57.383
He would put ethics aside to bring a research
project of his to perfection.

00:07:57.383 --> 00:08:04.063
I also think, that only a slightly messed
up person could bear not forgetting anything.

00:08:04.063 --> 00:08:05.763
Another drawback of this fruit.

00:08:05.763 --> 00:08:11.423
Our brains are hardwired to process and forget
about traumatic and hurtful events in our

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:12.433
life.

00:08:12.433 --> 00:08:18.993
Imagine you could never forget any accident
or terrible thing that happened in your life.

00:08:18.993 --> 00:08:25.113
Instead you can always recall it in perfect
detail.

00:08:25.113 --> 00:08:31.063
That sounds kind of unhealthy and in reality
would probably make life pretty much un-livable

00:08:31.063 --> 00:08:32.063
i think.

00:08:32.063 --> 00:08:36.173
What this means however, is that egg head
island IS a living part of Vegapunk.

00:08:36.173 --> 00:08:39.243
So why does he ask Luffy to take him away?

00:08:39.243 --> 00:08:41.583
Well there are a few possibilities.

00:08:41.583 --> 00:08:46.753
Maybe Vegapunk wants to go back to Elbaf,
where all of Ohara’s knowledge is stored.

00:08:46.753 --> 00:08:51.063
Maybe he wants to find Dragon, who is just
starting his big campaign with the revolutionaries,

00:08:51.063 --> 00:08:52.863
to help him in his fight.

00:08:52.863 --> 00:08:54.823
Or it could be that he is fearing for his
life.

00:08:54.823 --> 00:08:59.063
genius that he is, Vegapunk might already
have figured out, that the government is coming

00:08:59.063 --> 00:09:00.063
for his head.

00:09:00.063 --> 00:09:04.032
And Shaka has already talked to Dragon about
their soon to be expected death.

00:09:04.032 --> 00:09:08.743
So is it realistic, that we will leave Egghead
island with Vegapunk?

00:09:08.743 --> 00:09:12.603
Maybe even as the next, super unexpected straw
hat?

00:09:12.603 --> 00:09:14.602
I think there are arguments for both sides.

00:09:14.602 --> 00:09:18.383
I think you can’t really argue that Vegapunk
wouldn’t make a wonderful addition to the

00:09:18.383 --> 00:09:21.753
crew, travelling to Elbaf and finally laugh
Tale.

00:09:21.753 --> 00:09:27.133
It might be his knowledge and technology that’s
the key to reaching laugh tale and defeating

00:09:27.133 --> 00:09:29.042
the world government.

00:09:29.042 --> 00:09:32.222
Helping the straw hats reach their full potential
along the way.

00:09:32.222 --> 00:09:37.373
It would also be a great way to have Luffy
and Dragon reunite very soon.

00:09:37.373 --> 00:09:41.623
however, on the other hand, you could also
argue, that Vegapunk knows too much and is

00:09:41.623 --> 00:09:45.043
way too powerful to be an asset to Luffy.

00:09:45.043 --> 00:09:50.553
His knowledge about the world would make Robin
and especially Franky almost completley redundant

00:09:50.553 --> 00:09:51.673
in a way.

00:09:51.673 --> 00:09:56.023
It might also make the straw hats too powerful
going into the end game.

00:09:56.023 --> 00:10:01.833
Instead, giving Luffy and co SOME information
and a few upgrades, might be the safer route

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:06.472
to go for Oda, having Vegapunk actually die.

00:10:06.472 --> 00:10:10.352
And Dragon might be coming for Egghead island
anyways.

00:10:10.352 --> 00:10:16.423
The chapter suggests that Kuma is trying to
safe his daughter Bonney, after Lucci announced

00:10:16.423 --> 00:10:21.713
that they would kill her this time and that
she has no use anymore.

00:10:21.713 --> 00:10:27.513
Actually, now that i think about it, maybe
Bonney WAS the thing that the Gorosei used

00:10:27.513 --> 00:10:30.023
to blackmail Kuma and Vegapunk with.

00:10:30.023 --> 00:10:36.053
So maybe Kuma is actually also connected to
Vegapunks brain, the secret 7th clone.

00:10:36.053 --> 00:10:41.313
I think this chapter definitely gives us hope,
that we will see Kuma regain his real personalty

00:10:41.313 --> 00:10:45.842
though, especially since Vegapunk seems to
be very good with disconnecting brains and

00:10:45.842 --> 00:10:48.292
keeping them functioning.

00:10:48.292 --> 00:10:55.342
Kuma as a cyborg is already pretty damn impressive
as a feature of engineering, but not as impressive

00:10:55.342 --> 00:10:59.133
as the giant Robot soldier located on the
island.

00:10:59.133 --> 00:11:04.134
The manga has now finally confirmed, that
this is actually technology from the void

00:11:04.134 --> 00:11:05.134
century.

00:11:05.134 --> 00:11:11.333
However, it has been active a lot more recently
than we all expected.

00:11:11.333 --> 00:11:16.542
Instead of just rusting away there for the
past 800 years, apparently it climbed the

00:11:16.542 --> 00:11:21.363
red line in an attempt to attack Maris Jois.

00:11:21.363 --> 00:11:26.913
After it was stopped, government scientists
brought it to Egghead island to study it.

00:11:26.913 --> 00:11:32.243
And as expected its the inspiration for the
giant robot Vegapunk has built.

00:11:32.243 --> 00:11:35.233
Now this is fascinating for a few reasons.

00:11:35.233 --> 00:11:40.813
First: Someone actually remembered how to
use this technology 200 years ago and was

00:11:40.813 --> 00:11:43.423
able to use it against the government.

00:11:43.423 --> 00:11:49.003
Second: The government was able to stop this
thing somehow before they had any of Vegapunk’s

00:11:49.003 --> 00:11:50.003
inventions.

00:11:50.003 --> 00:11:55.643
And, as robin reminds us, it also fits in
perfectly with the time where the fishman

00:11:55.643 --> 00:12:00.222
were first acknowledged as people and not
fish and were invited to the Reverie.

00:12:00.222 --> 00:12:03.753
This is something that Hachi tells us about.

00:12:03.753 --> 00:12:09.003
now there are two other things that happened
200 years ago: that random ship that fell

00:12:09.003 --> 00:12:13.103
from the sky, had made it to Skypea during
that time.

00:12:13.103 --> 00:12:16.863
And the giant fighting fish appeared on green
bit.

00:12:16.863 --> 00:12:19.573
Could these events be connected?

00:12:19.573 --> 00:12:22.092
Really, no way of telling right now.

00:12:22.092 --> 00:12:27.563
But what Oda seems to suggest or at least
wants us to believe, is that the fishmen were

00:12:27.563 --> 00:12:33.513
the ones that send this giant robot to attack
the world government to get more rights.

00:12:33.513 --> 00:12:40.223
If so, Fisher Tiger, another fishman, might
have been foreshadowing for this.

00:12:40.223 --> 00:12:43.393
Maybe he was even inspired by his ancestors.

00:12:43.393 --> 00:12:48.213
Im very curious about what really happened
here.

00:12:48.213 --> 00:12:51.903
But let’s talk about the Robot’s mysterious
power source.

00:12:51.903 --> 00:12:56.972
It’s the second time now, that a Vegapunk
mentions a limitless energy source, an eternal

00:12:56.972 --> 00:13:01.712
flame, that was apparently used to power these
giant machines.

00:13:01.712 --> 00:13:06.712
I think some people suggested Franky’s Cola
technology, however, as we’ve seen more

00:13:06.712 --> 00:13:11.272
than once, it’s neither limitless nor very
convenient to use.

00:13:11.272 --> 00:13:15.753
Instead, it looks like the Robot has a giant
furnace as its belly.

00:13:15.753 --> 00:13:22.133
And the idea of an eternal flame does sound
a bit like something we are currently researching

00:13:22.133 --> 00:13:23.133
ourselves.

00:13:23.133 --> 00:13:28.902
You might be aware of nuclear power as splitting
atoms and using the energy stored inside their

00:13:28.902 --> 00:13:32.772
bonds, which creates a lot of dangerous radioactive
waste.

00:13:32.772 --> 00:13:40.842
However, you can also make energy by combining
lighter atoms into heavier ones under a lot

00:13:40.842 --> 00:13:41.842
of heat.

00:13:41.842 --> 00:13:46.613
This is called nuclear fusion, and it’s
basically how stars work.

00:13:46.613 --> 00:13:50.453
Our sun is one giant fusion reactor.

00:13:50.453 --> 00:13:55.342
And that technology exists, even if its not
yet ready for actual use quite yet.

00:13:55.342 --> 00:13:59.823
But since nuclear fusion is also referred
to as a sun in a bottle, that really made

00:13:59.823 --> 00:14:05.383
my alarm bells ring with all the sun god nika
talk lately.

00:14:05.383 --> 00:14:09.573
Luffy’s fire powers and the nika fruit’s
connection to the ancient kingdom and joy

00:14:09.573 --> 00:14:10.573
boy.

00:14:10.573 --> 00:14:15.893
So maybe one of the technologies that the
ancient kingdom used was nucelar fusion or

00:14:15.893 --> 00:14:20.532
the power of a sun slash sun god devil fruit.

00:14:20.532 --> 00:14:25.813
it’s one of the many lost technologies from
the void century, that have completely changed

00:14:25.813 --> 00:14:28.923
how we look at the one piece world and story.

00:14:28.923 --> 00:14:32.882
And i broke it all down in this video right
here, if you want to watch a little longer.

